A card or address fill whose confirmation nobody answered says how to ask again.

Symptom: the user did not see the fill confirmation within approvals.timeout
(300 s); browser_vault fill then answered payment_declined, "The user did not
confirm filling this payment card. Nothing was written. Do not retry; ask
them instead.", the same text as an explicit refusal. The agent took the
timeout for a refusal and gave up on the purchase.

Fix (hyperhermes): `_confirm_payment_fill` returns the decision
(accept/decline/cancel); a `cancel` (request_elicitation_consent's "nobody
answered": timeout, or the prompt withdrawn) answers payment_unanswered,
naming the timeout, that nothing was written, and that a fill with the same
handle once the user is back asks anew. A refusal stays payment_declined with
"Do not retry". The timeout itself stays approvals.timeout (300 s default;
the gateway's prompt holds the turn that long, and a fill ask is one tap).
Not upstream.

